  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-saving response through the provision of emergency shelter and non-food items to returnees from the SudanLife-saving response through the provision of emergency shelter and non-food items to returnees from the Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the onset of the Sudan conflict in April 2023, an estimated 892,139 people have crossed into South Sudan (UNHCR/IOM dashboard, 12 December 2024). The influx of arrivals from Sudan has created additional strain on the humanitarian response and overwhelmed coping capacities in host communities. IOM is procuring and prepositioning emergency Shelter Non-Food Item (SNFI) kits at its Bentiu and Wau warehouses, ensuring access for SNFI Cluster partners operating in Kirr Adem and Majokyinthiou. The kits are comprised of plastic sheets, rubber rope, blankets, mosquito nets and sleeping mats. The kit composition will enable the returnee households to quickly construct emergency shelters, access to bedding and ensure prevention of malaria and any other cold related diseases such as pneumonia especially among the children under five.</narrative>
  </description>
